The reference audit shows a subtle but important constraint: the catalogue’s destinations are not arbitrary. At any seed it needs the best evaluated one-user alternative for each user, but it only emits configurations changing at least two users. For A3/A4 I’ll preserve that exact destination scan while never adopting a unilateral move; its evaluation cost will be charged to those arms. The served-count guard will be the selection-time BASELINE served count for every arm and every A4 round, matching A2. I’m declaring A4’s cap now as 16 catalogue rounds, with a terminal round defined as the first round yielding no strict objective improvement.
